<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>debug &mdash; <%= @playthrough&.story&.title %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%# ITS OWN STYLESHEET, and that is the point of it being a separate layout.
        The reading experience is deliberately deferred (`ta-api-iface`), so this
        page must not be able to change how the story reads -- the two share no
        CSS at all. Inline for the same reason the game's is: no propshaft, no
        importmap, no build step.

        Dense and unapologetically technical. Wider than the game's 44rem
        because tables of connections do not wrap usefully. %>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: dark; }
      body {
        background: #0d0f12; color: #b8c0c8;
        font: 13px/1.5 ui-monospace, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
        margin: 0; padding: 1.5rem 1rem 6rem;
      }
      main { max-width: 76rem; margin: 0 auto; }
      a { color: #7fb2d8; }
      h1 {
        font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #d8c07f; margin: 0 0 .25rem;
      }
      h2 {
        font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #6f8ba4; margin: 2rem 0 .5rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #21262c; padding-bottom: .3rem;
      }
      h3 { font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8b939b; margin: 1rem 0 .35rem; }
      .nav { color: #6b737b; margin: 0 0 1rem; }

      /* Every panel is a bordered block; the current turn is the one that gets
         an accent, because the whole view is organised around it. */
      .panel { border: 1px solid #21262c; padding: .6rem .8rem; margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
      .panel.now { border-color: #4a4326; background: #14140f; }

      /* label / value pairs. Grid rather than a table so a long value wraps
         under its own label instead of stretching the column. */
      .fields { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 11rem) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .15rem .8rem; }
      .fields > .k { color: #6b737b; }
      .fields > .v { color: #cfd3d8; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

      .absent { color: #7a6a52; font-style: italic; }
      .prose { white-space: pre-wrap; color: #cfd3d8; }
      .note { color: #6b737b; margin: .2rem 0 .6rem; }
      .warn { color: #d88f7f; }

      pre {
        background: #08090b; border: 1px solid #21262c; color: #9aa3ac;
        padding: .5rem .6rem; margin: .3rem 0 0; overflow-x: auto;
        white-space: pre; font: inherit;
      }

      /* Wide content scrolls inside its own box; the page body never does. */
      .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
      table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 12px; }
      th, td { text-align: left; padding: .25rem .5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1e23; vertical-align: top; }
      th { color: #6b737b; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 11px; }
      tbody tr:hover { background: #12151a; }

      /* The branch a turn took, coloured so a long log can be scanned. Purple
         for a model call the player reads, teal for the app deciding -- the
         same colours the README's turn diagram uses. */
      .branch { padding: 0 .35rem; border: 1px solid; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 11px; }
      .branch.arrival { color: #b79ad8; border-color: #4a3d5c; }
      .branch.conversation { color: #7fd8c0; border-color: #2f5a50; }
      .branch.narration { color: #d8c07f; border-color: #5c5326; }
      .branch.opening { color: #8b939b; border-color: #33393f; }

      .tag { color: #8b939b; border: 1px solid #33393f; padding: 0 .3rem; font-size: 11px; }
      .tag.stub { color: #7a6a52; border-color: #4a3f2e; }
      .tag.realized { color: #7fd8c0; border-color: #2f5a50; }
      .tag.mobile { color: #b79ad8; border-color: #4a3d5c; }

      ul.evidence { margin: .3rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; color: #8b939b; }
      ul.evidence li { margin: .05rem 0; }

      details { margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
      details > summary { cursor: pointer; color: #9aa3ac; padding: .15rem 0; }
      details > summary:hover { color: #cfd3d8; }
      details[open] > summary { color: #cfd3d8; }
      details .body { padding: .4rem 0 .8rem 1rem; border-left: 1px solid #21262c; margin-left: .3rem; }

      /* Narrow: the label column costs more than it buys, so the pairs stack.
         Tables keep their own horizontal scroll, so nothing here widens the
         page. */
      @media (max-width: 40rem) {
        .fields { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0; }
        .fields > .k { color: #6f8ba4; margin-top: .5rem; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main><%= yield %></main>
  </body>
</html>
